messages.body_plain:
Hi Folks,

I've been playing around with OpenMP recently, to see if I can speed up 
some ergm code. My code compiles just fine, although R crashes when I 
try to run OMP-enabled analyses e.g. here's the code for d_edges in 
changestats.c

D_CHANGESTAT_FN(d_edges) {
  int edgeflag, i;
  Vertex h, t;

  CHANGE_STAT[0] = 0.0;
  #pragma omp parallel for shared(ntoggles,nwp,mtp) 
private(i,h,t,edgeflag,heads,tails)
  for (i=0; i < ntoggles; i++)
    {
      edgeflag = IS_OUTEDGE(h = heads[i], t = tails[i]);
      CHANGE_STAT[0] += edgeflag ? - 1 : 1;
      TOGGLE_IF_MORE_TO_COME(i);
    }
  UNDO_PREVIOUS_TOGGLES(i);
}

With gcc, the Makevars file is

PKG_LIBS=-fopenmp -lgomp -lpthread
PKG_CFLAGS=-fopenmp

The obfuscating macros don't help for me to see which should be shared 
and which should be private. I know that only certain proposals will 
benefit from multithreading here, but I'm unfamiliar with the statnet 
API, I wanted to know whether the code was thread-safe, and if so, 
whether multithreading may belong elsewhere in the code.

Best
Simon
